{
  "about": [
    "Patterns for the functional-group highlighter (docs/SPEC.md, section 3). Edit freely: no code change is needed, and the tests check this file (web/src/chem/functionalGroups.test.ts).",
    "Each group has a name (shown in the panel), smarts (RDKit SMARTS), color (#rrggbb, drawn behind the atoms) and priority (a number; higher wins).",
    "Every atom the SMARTS matches belongs to the group: it is coloured, and no lower-priority group may use it. Atoms that only have to be nearby go inside $(...), so an alcohol is its O and an ester its C(=O)O.",
    "Groups are applied from the highest priority down. A match that needs an atom a higher-priority group already has is dropped (an ester's O is not also an ether). Matches of one group that share atoms count as one."
  ],
  "groups": [
